<header><p class="enc-kicker"><a href="/encyclopedia/conflicts/13th-century">Conflicts &amp; Resolutions</a> · Battle</p><h1 class="enc-title">Battle of al-Mansurah</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates"><a href="/years/1250">1250</a></span> · <a href="/centuries/13th-century">13th century</a> · Also known as Battle of Mansourah · Part of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/seventh-crusade">Seventh Crusade</a></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">The Battle of al-Mansurah was fought in February 1250 in the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/nile-delta">Nile Delta</a> of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/egypt">Egypt</a> during the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/seventh-crusade">Seventh Crusade</a> led by <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/louis-ix-of-france">Louis IX of France</a>. <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/crusader-states">Crusaders</a> under the king's brother Robert of Artois charged into the town of al-Mansurah, where they were trapped and killed by Ayyubid and <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/mamluk">Mamluk</a> troops, among them <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/baybars">Baybars</a>. The <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/crusade">crusade</a> ended with Louis's capture at Fariskur in April.</p></div>
